    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Josh Naylor** (77.76) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) headline our offensive assault, both capitalizing on a prime matchup against the shaky arm of Littell and Imai respectively. **Josh Naylor** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and an favorable park environment, solidifying his role as our primary run producer. **Corbin Carroll** (71.84) also grades out as an elite start; while he faces a slight platoon disadvantage against Lodolo, his inherent speed and the +8% boost from batting second provide a high floor for SB production, which remains our primary objective in this scoring environment.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Brice Turang** (49.77), who narrowly missed the cut behind the superior daily efficiency of **Jose Caballero** and **Seiya Suzuki**. Despite **Brice Turang** offering speed, the high quality of the opposing catcher's pop time (1.86s) significantly dampens his stolen base equity compared to our active starters. We are also closely monitoring the lineup for **Seiya Suzuki**; we have projected him at the five-hole, but his final score is contingent on that placement holding. With **Mickey Moniak** remaining sidelined on the IL, our roster depth is being tested, but the efficiency scores confirm that sticking with our active 12\u2014led by the high-upside profiles of **James Wood** and **Gabriel Moreno**\u2014provides the best statistical path to securing our categories today.",
